fix: keep a user type named K out of Record's key variable and let type parameters shadow outer aliases
Record<'a' | 'b', K> bound its key variable under the name K, so a user type K in the value position resolved to the key. A type parameter in scope also lost to a module-level alias of the same name for plain references while function-type members kept the parameter.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013R2ytvK9B32ZaSUaSe6aAZ
